DESC Component identification preamble, segment 3
R 0xd900 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_event_sel
RESET 0x800000000000 0x7fffff7f7f7f7f
DESC Specifies the PMU event to be counted.
F 0 7 pmu_event0_id
DESC HN-S PMU Event 0 select 7'h00: No event 7'h01: PMU_HN_CACHE_MISS_EVENT; counts total cache misses in first lookup result. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h02: PMU_HN_SLCSF_CACHE_ACCESS_LOOKUP_EVENT; counts number of cache accesses in first access (high priority). Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h03: PMU_HN_CACHE_FILL_EVENT; counts total allocations in HN SLC (all cache line allocations to SLC). Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h04: PMU_HN_POCQ_RETRY_EVENT; counts number of retried requests. Filtering is programmed in pmu_occup1_id (Rxsnp request cannot be retied and the event should be 0 if the filter is selected) 7'h05: PMU_HN_POCQ_REQS_RECVD_EVENT; counts number of requests received by HN. Filtering is programmed in pmu_occup1_id 7'h06: PMU_HN_SF_HIT_EVENT; counts number of SF hits. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h07: PMU_HN_SF_EVICTIONS_EVENT; counts number of SF eviction cache invalidations initiated for specific SF state. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel and pmu_evict_state_sel(MU/MN states are not applicable and event should be 0 if the filter is selected) 7'h08: PMU_HN_DIR_SNOOPS_SENT_EVENT; counts number of directed snoops sent (not including SF back invalidation). Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h09: PMU_HN_BRD_SNOOPS_SENTEVENT; counts number of multicast snoops send (not including SF back invalidation). Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h0A: PMU_HN_SLC_EVICTION_EVENT; counts number of SLC evictions for specific SLC state. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel and pmu_evict_state_sel 7'h0B: PMU_HN_SLC_FILL_INVALID_WAY_EVENT; counts number of SLC fills to an invalid way. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h0C: PMU_HN_MC_RETRIES_LOCAL_EVENT; counts number of local retried transactions by the MC. Filtering is programmed in pmu_sn_home_sel 7'h0D: PMU_HN_MC_REQS_LOCAL_EVENT; counts number of local requests sent to MC. Filtering is programmed in pmu_sn_home_sel 7'h0E: PMU_HN_QOS_HH_RETRY_EVENT; counts number of times a HighHigh priority request is protocol retried at the HN-S 7'h0F: PMU_HN_POCQ_OCCUPANCY_EVENT; counts the POCQ occupancy in HN-S; occupancy filtering is programmed in pmu_occup1_id 7'h10: PMU_HN_POCQ_ADDRHAZ_EVENT; counts number of POCQ address hazards upon allocation. Filterfing is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h11: PMU_HN_POCQ_ATOMICS_ADDRHAZ_EVENT; counts number of POCQ address hazards upon allocation for atomic operations . Filterfing is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h12: PMU_HN_LD_ST_SWP_ADQ_FULL_EVENT; counts number of times ADQ is full for Ld/St/SWP type atomic operations while POCQ has pending operations 7'h13: PMU_HN_CMP_ADQ_FULL_EVENT; counts number of times ADQ is full for CMP type atomic operations while POCQ has pending operations 7'h14: PMU_HN_TXDAT_STALL_EVENT; counts number of times HN-S has a pending TXDAT flit but no credits to upload 7'h15: PMU_HN_TXRSP_STALL_EVENT; counts number of times HN-S has a pending TXRSP flit but no credits to upload 7'h16: PMU_HN_SEQ_FULL_EVENT; counts number of times requests are replayed in SLC pipe due to SEQ being full 7'h17: PMU_HN_SEQ_HIT_EVENT; counts number of times a request in SLC hit a pending SF eviction in SEQ 7'h18: PMU_HN_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of snoops sent including directed/multicast/SF back invalidation. Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h19: PMU_HN_SFBI_DIR_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of times directed snoops were sent due to SF back invalidation. Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h1a: PMU_HN_SFBI_BRD_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of times multicast snoops were sent due to SF back invalidation. Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h1b: Reserved 7'h1c: PMU_HN_INTV_DIRTY_EVENT; counts number of times SF back invalidation resulted in dirty line intervention from the RN 7'h1d: PMU_HN_STASH_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of times stash snoops sent 7'h1e: PMU_HN_STASH_DATA_PULL_EVENT; counts number of times stash snoops resulted in data pull from the RN 7'h1f: PMU_HN_SNP_FWDED_EVENT; counts any forward type snoops sent. Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h20: PMU_HN_ATOMIC_FWD_EVENT; counts number of times atomic data was forwarded between POC entries 7'h21: PMU_HN_MPAM_REQ_OVER_HARDLIM_EVENT; counts number of times write req can't allocate in SLC due to being over hardlimit. Filtering is programmed in cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask 7'h22: PMU_HN_MPAM_REQ_OVER_SOFTLIM_EVENT; counts number of times write req is above soft limit. Filtering is programmed in cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask 7'h23: PMU_HN_SNP_SENT_CLUSTER_EVENT; counts number of snoops sent to clusters excluding indivual snoops within a cluster. Filtering is programmed in pmu_snp_vc_sel 7'h24: PMU_HN_SF_IMPRECISE_EVICT_EVENT; counts number of times an evict op was dropped due to SF clustering. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h25: PMU_HN_SF_EVICT_SHARED_LINE_EVENT; counts number of times a shared line was evicted from SF 7'h26: PMU_HN_POCQ_CLASS_OCCUPANCY_EVENT; counts the POCQ occupancy for a given class in HN-S; Class occupancy filtering is programmed in pmu_class_occup_id 7'h27: PMU_HN_POCQ_CLASS_RETRY_EVENT; counts number of retried requests for a given class; Class filtering is programmed in pmu_class_occup_id 7'h28: PMU_HN_CLASS_MC_REQS_LOCAL_EVENT; counts number of local requests sent to MC for a given class; Class filtering is programmed in pmu_class_occup_id 7'h29: PMU_HN_CLASS_PCRDGNT_BELOW_CONDMIN_EVENT; counts number of protocol credit grants for a given class when it's above dedicated and below conditional min; Class filtering is programmed in pmu_class_occup_id 7'h2A: PMU_HN_NUM_SN_CBUSY_THROTTLE_EVENT; counts number of times request to SN was throttled due to cbusy; Event filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h2B: PMU_HN_NUM_SN_CBUSY_THROTTLE_MIN_EVENT; counts number of times request to SN was throttled to the minimum allowed value of 4, due to cbusy; Event filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h2C: PMU_HN_SF_PRECISE_TO_IMPRECISE_EVENT; counts when number sharers exceeds how many RN's could be precisely tracked in SF 7'h2D: PMU_HN_SNP_INTV_CLN_EVENT; counts the number of times clean data intervened for a snoop request 7'h2E: PMU_HN_NC_EXCL_EVENT; counts the number of times non-cacheable exclusive request arrived at HNS 7'h2F: Reserved 7'h30: PMU_HN_SNP_REQ_RECVD_EVENT; counts number of incoming snoop requests 7'h31: PMU_HN_SNP_REQ_BYP_POCQ_EVENT; counts number of times incoming snoop request bypass Snoop Queue and allocates in POCQ 7'h32: PMU_HN_DIR_CCGHA_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of directed snoops sent to CCG HA. (SFBI and non-SFBI included). 7'h33: PMU_HN_BRD_CCGHA_SNP_SENT_EVENT; counts number of broadcast snoops sent to CCG HA. (SFBI and non-SFBI included). 7'h34: PMU_HN_CCGHA_SNP_STALL_EVENT; counts number of times snoop is ready to be sent to CCG HA but stalled due to maximum snoops allowed. 7'h35: PMU_HN_LBT_REQ_OVER_HARDLIM_EVENT; counts number of times LBT write req can't allocate in SLC due to being over LBT cache capacity 7'h36: PMU_HN_HBT_REQ_OVER_HARDLIM_EVENT; counts number of times HBT write req can't allocate in SLC due to being over HBT cache capacity 7'h37: PMU_HN_SF_REUPDATE_EVENT; counts number of times SF needs to be re-updated 7'h38: PMU_HN_EXCL_SF_IMPRECISE_EVENT; counts number of times exclusive req hits SF in imprecise mode. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h39: PMU_HN_SNP_POCQ_ADDRHAZ_EVENT; counts number of POCQ address hazards involving external snoop requests at allocation 7'h3A: PMU_HN_MC_RETRIES_REMOTE_EVENT; counts number of remote retried transactions by the MC. Filtering is programmed in pmu_sn_home_sel 7'h3B: PMU_HN_MC_REQS_REMOTE_EVENT; counts number of remote requests sent to MC. Filtering is programmed in pmu_sn_home_sel 7'h3C: PMU_HN_CLASS_MC_REQS_REMOTE_EVENT; counts number of remote requests sent to MC for a given class; Class filtering is programmed in pmu_class_occup_id 7'h3D: PMU_HN_READONCE_HAZARD_DETECTED_EVENT; Dependent RdOnce or RNSD eligible for forwarding. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h3E: PMU_HN_READONCE_FWD_DATA_COMPLETED_EVENT; Dependent RdOnce or RNSD entry got forwarded data. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h3F: PMU_HN_SFBI_FILL_EVENT; Counts number of cache fills caused by SF back invalidation. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h40: PMU_HN_CBUSY00_EVENT; Monitor CBUSY 00 is executed. Filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h41: PMU_HN_CBUSY01_EVENT; Monitor CBUSY 01 is executed. Filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h42: PMU_HN_CBUSY10_EVENT; Monitor CBUSY 10 is executed. Filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h43: PMU_HN_CBUSY11_EVENT; Monitor CBUSY 11 is executed. Filtering is programmed in pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel 7'h44: PMU_HN_READONCE_FWD_ELIGIBLE_EVENT; Counts request transactions that are eligible for RdOnce optimization. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h45: PMU_HN_SHD_INTV_EVENT. Counts number of shared interventions. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h46: PMU_HN_SNP_INTV_FILL_EVENT. Counts number of fill due to any snoop intervention. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h47: PMU_HN_RN_GET_OWNER_FROM_SHD_EVENT. Counts number of RNF asking for cacheline ownership from shared state. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h48: PMU_HN_IMPRECISE_TO_PRECISE_REQ. Counts when anytime SF entry goes from Imprecise to Precise due to request. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h49: PMU_HN_SFEVICT_IMPRECISE. Counts when anytime imprecise SF entry is back invalidated due to capacity eviction. Filtering is programmed in pmu_hbt_lbt_sel 7'h4A: PMU_HN_WEOEASEVICT_L3MISS. Counts WEOE op treated as EVICT incurs an L3Miss and SF is not being invalidated. Filtering is programmed in pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel (except RNI). Not applicable to OCM region
F 8 7 pmu_event1_id
DESC HN-F PMU Event 1 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 16 7 pmu_event2_id
DESC HN-F PMU Event 2 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 24 7 pmu_event3_id
DESC HN-F PMU Event 3 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 32 4 pmu_occup1_id
DESC HN-F PMU occupancy 1 select 4'b0000: All occupancy selected 4'b0001: Read requests 4'b0010: Write requests 4'b0011: Atomic operation requests 4'b0100: Stash requests 4'b0101: RxSnp requests 4'b0110: LBT requests 4'b0111: HBT requests 4'b1000: All requests from local RNF 4'b1001: All requests from lcal RNI 4'b1010: All requests from CCG-LCN 4'b1011: All requests from CCG RNI/RNF 4'b1100: All requests from local LCNs 4'b1101: MPAM (for NE/CPU)
F 36 2 pmu_class_occup_id
DESC HN-F PMU Class select 2'b00: Class 0 selected 2'b01: Class 1 selected 2'b10: Class 2 selected 2'b11: Class 3 selected
F 38 2 pmu_hbt_lbt_sel
DESC HN-F PMU HBT/LBT select 2'b00: All requests selected 2'b01: HBT requests selected 2'b10: LBT requests selected
F 40 2 pmu_sn_home_sel
DESC HN-F PMU SN/Home select 2'b00: All requests selected 2'b01: SN bound requests selected 2'b10: Remote home bound requests selected 2'b11: Local home bound requests selected
F 42 4 pmu_cbusy_snthrottle_sel
DESC Filter for selecting specific SN throttle type 4'b0000: All SN types throttled 4'b0001: SN Group 0 Reads 4'b0010: SN Group 0 Non-Reads 4'b0011: SN Group 1 Reads 4'b0100: SN Group 1 Non-Reads 4'b0101: All SN Reads 4'b0110: All SN Non-Reads 4'b0111: Local HNF Reads 4'b1000: Local HNF Non-Reads 4'b1001: Remote CCG Reads 4'b1010: Remote CCG Non-Reads 4'b1011: All LBT Reads 4'b1100: All LBT Non-Reads 4'b1101: All LBT throttled
F 46 2 pmu_snp_vc_sel
DESC HN-S PMU Snoop VC select when 3TXSNP channels are enabled 2'b00: Snoop VC0 to CCG 2'b01: Snoop VC1 to local LCNs 2'b10: Snoop VC2 to local RNFs 2'b11: Reserved HN-S PMU Snoop VC select when 2TXSNP channels are enabled 2'b00: Snoop VC0 to HBT 2'b01: Snoop VC1 to LBT 2'b10: Reserved 2'b11: Reserved
F 48 4 pmu_enhanced_hbt_lbt_sel
DESC HN-F PMU enhanced hbt/lbt/source select 4'b0000: All occupancy selected 4'b0001: HBT requests 4'b0010: LBT requests 4'b0011: All requests from local RNF 4'b0100: All requests from local RNI 4'b0101: All requests from CCG-LCN 4'b0110: All requests from CCG RNI/RNF 4'b0111: All requests from local LCNs 4'b1000: MPAM (for NE/CPU)
F 52 3 pmu_evict_state_sel
DESC HN-F SF/SLC Eviction data state select 3'b000: All state 3'b001: State EU 3'b010: State EN 3'b011: State SU 3'b100: State SN 3'b101: State MU 3'b110: State MN 
R 0xd908 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel
RESET 0x8 0x1e
DESC Specifies details of MPAM event to be counted
F 1 1 pmu_mpam_hardlim_sel
DESC When set, HN-F PMU MPAM Hardlimit count is filtered for specific PARTIDs 1'b0: PMU Hardlimit count is total for all PARDIDs. 1'b1: PMU Hardlimit count is only for PARDIDs indicated in fliter register
F 2 1 pmu_mpam_softlim_sel
DESC When set, HN-F PMU MPAM Softlimit count is filtered for specific PARTIDs 1'b0: PMU Softlimit count is total for all PARDIDs. 1'b1: PMU Softlimit count is only for PARDIDs indicated in fliter register
F 3 2 pmu_mpam_pas_mask_sel
DESC PAS select for PARTID Mask 2'b00: PMU MPAM mask is for Secure MPAMID. 2'b01: PMU MPAM mask is for Non-Secure MPAMID. 2'b10: PMU MPAM mask is for Root MPAMID. 2'b11: PMU MPAM mask is for Realm MPAMID.
R 0xd910 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask0
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[63:0] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask0
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [63:0] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd918 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask1
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[127:64] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask1
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [127:64] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd920 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask2
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[191:128] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask2
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [191:128] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd928 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask3
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[255:192] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask3
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [255:192] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd930 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask4
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[319:256] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask4
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [319:256] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd938 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask5
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[383:320] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask5
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [383:320] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xd940 64 - - cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_pardid_mask6
RESET 0x0 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Functions as mask for PARTID[447:384] filter for MPM PMU events
F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask6
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [447:384] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
