F 0 64 pmu_mpam_partid_mask7
DESC MPAM PMU hardlimit and softlimit mask for PARTID [511:448] 1'b0: PARTID specified is not counted in PMU count. 1'b1: PARTID specified is counted in PMU count. Note: This mask is used only when cmn_hns_pmu_mpam_sel is set for PARTID based counting.
R 0xe000 64 RO ROOT cmn_hns_errfr
RESET 0x5200008012c9a2 0x720000803ffff3
DESC Functions as the error feature register.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras
F 0 2 ed
DESC Error reporting and logging control 2'b10: Error reporting and logging is controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.ED
F 4 2 ui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt on Uncorrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.UI.
F 6 2 fi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on Deferred and Uncorrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.FI.
F 8 2 ue
DESC In-band error response is always on
F 10 2 cfi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on corrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.CFI.
F 12 3 cec
DESC Standard corrected error counter 3'b000: Does not implement standard error counter model 3'b100: Implements a 16-bit Corrected error counter in cmn_hns_errmisc0
F 15 1 rp
DESC Repeat counter (valid only when cmn_hns_errfr.CEC != 3'b000.) 1'b0: Invalid; 1'b1: Implements a first (repeat) counter and a second (other) counter in cmn_hns_errmisc0
F 16 2 dui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.DUI.
F 18 2 ceo
DESC Corrected Error overwrite. 2'b00: Keep the first Corrected Error syndrome
F 20 2 inj
DESC Fault Injection Extension. 2'b01: Support Common Fault Injection Model Extension
F 31 1 frx
DESC Feature Register extension. 1'b1: cmn_hns_errfr[63:48] is architecturally defined
F 49 1 ueu
DESC Unrecoverable Error recording 1'b0: Unrecoverable Error not supported 1'b1: Unrecoverable Error supported
F 52 1 de
DESC Deferred Error recording 1'b0: Deferred Error not supported 1'b1: Deffered Error supported
F 53 2 ce
DESC Corrected Error recording 2'b00: Corrected Error not supported 2'b10: Non-specific Corrected Error supported
R 0xe008 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_errctlr
RESET 0x0 0x10000050d
DESC Functions as the error control register. Controls whether specific error-handling interrupts and error detection/deferment are enabled.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras
F 0 1 ed
DESC Enables error detection as specified in cmn_hns_errfr.ED
F 2 1 ui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for uncorrected error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr.UI
F 3 1 fi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for uncorrected and deferred errors as specified in cmn_hns_errfr.FI
F 8 1 cfi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for corrected error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr.CFI
F 10 1 dui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for deferred error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr.DUI
F 32 1 par_err_en
DESC Enables external logging parity errors when set to 1'b1
R 0xe010 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_errstatus
RESET 0x0 0xfff0ffff
DESC Functions as the error status register. When V is set, only write exact same value as in the register can clear it.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras
F 31 1 av W1C
DESC Address register valid 1'b1: Address is valid; cmn_hns_erraddr contains a physical address for that recorded error 1'b0: Address is not valid
F 30 1 v W1C
DESC Status register valid 1'b1: At least one error recorded; register is valid 1'b0: No errors recorded
F 29 1 ue W1C
DESC Uncorrected errors 1'b1: At least one error detected that is not corrected and is not deferred to a subordinate 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected
F 28 1 er W1C
DESC Error Reported 1'b1: In-band error response signaled to the Requester 1'b0: No in-band error response signaled
F 27 1 of W1C
DESC Overflow; asserted when multiple errors are detected 1'b1: More than one error detected 1'b0: None or only one error detected as described by UE/DE/CE fields
F 26 1 mv W1C
DESC cmn_hns_errmisc<01> valid 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 2 ce W1C
DESC Corrected errors 2'b10: At least one corrected error recorded 2'b00: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 de W1C
DESC Deferred errors 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
F 22 1 pn W1C
DESC Poison 1'b1: Uncorrected error recorded because a poison value was consumed 1'b0: Other cases
F 20 2 uet W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error Type, valid only when UE != 0 2'b01: Uncorrected error, Unrecoverable error (UEU). 2'b00: Invalid
F 8 8 ierr W1C
DESC Implementation-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: Partner implementation defined error
F 0 8 serr W1C
DESC Architecturally-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: CMN implementation defined error. Refer to cmn_hns_errmisc1.ERRSRC for error type details. 8'h06: ECC error on L3 data 8'h07: ECC error on L3/SF Tag 8'h0A: Producer write data was poisoned but ACE-Lite does not support poisoned data 8'h0D: Illegal address 8'h1A: Parity error
R 0xe018 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_erraddr
RESET 0x0 0xc80fffffffffffff
DESC Contains the error record address.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras
F 0 52 addr
DESC Transaction address
F 59 1 nse
DESC Root status of transaction.  PAS[1] of the transaction.
F 62 1 si
DESC {NSE,NS} valid 1'b0: PAS field is valid 1'b1: PAS field is invalid
F 63 1 ns
DESC Security status of transaction.  PAS[0] of the transaction.
R 0xe020 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_errmisc0
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff00000000
DESC Functions as miscellaneous error register 0. Contains information about corrected errors.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 63 1 ofo
DESC Corrected error counter overflow
F 48 15 ceco
DESC Corrected ECC error count
F 47 1 ofr
DESC Corrected error counter overflow
F 32 15 cecr
DESC Corrected ECC error count
R 0xe028 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_errmisc1
RESET 0x0 0x5fff00004ff37fff
DESC Functions as the miscellaneous error register. Contains miscellaneous information about deferred/uncorrected errors.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 4 11 srcid
DESC Error source ID
F 16 2 optype
DESC Error op type 2'b00: Writes, CleanShared, Atomics and stash requests with invalid targets 2'b01: WriteBack, Evict, and Stash requests with valid target 2'b10: CMO 2'b11: Other op types
F 20 8 errway
DESC SLC/SF way ID for ECC error
F 30 1 multiwayerr
DESC Indicate multiple ways have ECC error
F 48 13 errset
DESC SLC/SF set address for ECC error
F 62 1 setmatch
DESC Set address match
F 0 4 errsrc
DESC Error source 4'b0001: Data single-bit ECC 4'b0010: Data double-bit ECC 4'b0011: Single-bit ECC overflow 4'b0100: Tag single-bit ECC 4'b0101: Tag double-bit ECC 4'b0111: SF tag single-bit ECC 4'b1000: SF tag double-bit ECC 4'b1010: Data parity error 4'b1011: Data parity and poison 4'b1100: NDE
R 0xe030 64 - ROOT cmn_hns_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x7ff01f1
DESC Enables error injection and setup. When enabled for a given source ID and logic processor ID, HN-F returns a subordinate error and reports an error interrupt. This error interrupt emulates a SLC double-bit data ECC error. This feature enables software to test the error handler. The subordinate error is reported for cacheable read access for which SLC hit is the data source. No subordinate error or error interrupt is reported for cacheable read access in which SLC miss is the data source.
RGO cmn_hns_rcr.ras
SGO cmn_hns_scr.ras
F 0 1 err_inj_en
DESC Enables error injection and report
F 4 5 err_inj_lpid
DESC LPID used to match for error injection
F 16 11 err_inj_srcid
DESC RN source ID for read access which results in a SLC miss; does not report subordinate error or error to match error injection
R 0xe040 64 RO - cmn_hns_errfr_ns
RESET 0x5200008012c9a2 0x720000803ffff3
DESC Functions as the non-secure error feature register.
F 0 2 ed
DESC Error reporting and logging control 2'b10: Error reporting and logging is controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.ED
F 4 2 ui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt on Uncorrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.UI.
F 6 2 fi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on Deferred and Uncorrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.FI.
F 8 2 ue
DESC In-band error response is always on
F 10 2 cfi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on corrected errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.CFI.
F 12 3 cec
DESC Standard corrected error counter 3'b000: Does not implement standard error counter model 3'b100: Implements a 16-bit Corrected error counter in cmn_hns_errmisc0
F 15 1 rp
DESC Repeat counter (valid only when cmn_hns_errfr_NS.CEC != 3'b000.) 1'b1: Implements a first (repeat) counter and a second (other) counter in cmn_hns_errmisc0
F 16 2 dui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors and controllable using cmn_hns_errctlr.DUI.
F 18 2 ceo
DESC Corrected Error overwrite. 2'b00: Keep the first Corrected Error syndrome
F 20 2 inj
DESC Fault Injection Extension. 2'b01: Support Common Fault Injection Model Extension
F 31 1 frx
DESC Feature Register extension. 1'b1: cmn_hns_errfr_NS[63:48] is architecturally defined
F 49 1 ueu
DESC Unrecoverable Error recording 1'b0: Unrecoverable Error not supported 1'b1: Unrecoverable Error supported
F 52 1 de
DESC Deferred Error recording 1'b0: Deferred Error not supported 1'b1: Deffered Error supported
F 53 2 ce
DESC Corrected Error recording 2'b00: Corrected Error not supported 2'b10: Non-specific Corrected Error supported
R 0xe048 64 - - cmn_hns_errctlr_ns
RESET 0x0 0x50d
DESC Functions as the non-secure error control register. Controls whether specific error-handling interrupts and error detection/deferment are enabled.
F 0 1 ed
DESC Enables error detection as specified in cmn_hns_errfr_NS.ED
F 2 1 ui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for uncorrected error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr_NS.UI
F 3 1 fi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for uncorrected and deferred errors as specified in cmn_hns_errfr_NS.FI
F 8 1 cfi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for corrected error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr_NS.CFI
F 10 1 dui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for deferred error as specified in cmn_hns_errfr_NS.DUI
R 0xe050 64 - - cmn_hns_errstatus_ns
RESET 0x0 0xfff0ffff
DESC Functions as the non-secure error status register. When V is set, only write exact same value as in the register can clear it.
F 31 1 av W1C
DESC Address register valid 1'b1: Address is valid; cmn_hns_erraddr contains a physical address for that recorded error 1'b0: Address is not valid
F 30 1 v W1C
DESC Status register valid 1'b1: At least one error recorded; register is valid 1'b0: No errors recorded
F 29 1 ue W1C
DESC Uncorrected errors 1'b1: At least one error detected that is not corrected and is not deferred to a subordinate 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected
F 28 1 er W1C
DESC Error Reported 1'b1: In-band error response signaled to the Requester 1'b0: No in-band error response signaled
F 27 1 of W1C
DESC Overflow; asserted when multiple errors are detected 1'b1: More than one error detected 1'b0: None or only one error detected as described by UE/DE/CE fields
F 26 1 mv W1C
DESC cmn_hns_errmisc<01> valid 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 2 ce W1C
DESC Corrected errors 2'b10: At least one corrected error recorded 2'b00: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 de W1C
DESC Deferred errors 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
F 22 1 pn W1C
DESC Poison 1'b1: Uncorrected error recorded because a poison value was consumed 1'b0: Other cases
F 20 2 uet W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error Type, valid only when UE != 0 2'b01: Uncorrected error, Unrecoverable error (UEU). 2'b00: Invalid
F 8 8 ierr W1C
DESC Implementation-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: Partner implementation defined error
F 0 8 serr W1C
DESC Architecturally-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: CMN implementation defined error. Refer to cmn_hns_errmisc1_NS.ERRSRC for error type details. 8'h06: ECC error on cache data 8'h07: ECC error on L3/SF Tag 8'h0A: Producer write data was poisoned but ACE-Lite does not support poisoned data 8'h0D: Illegal address 8'h1A: Parity error
