RESET 0x0 0xf
DESC Secure Control Registers for predefined groups of root registers.
F 0 1 ldid_ctl
DESC Secure Control Register for root HA LDID registers
F 1 1 linkid_ctl
DESC Secure Control Register for root HA Link ID registers
F 2 1 mpam_ctl
DESC Secure Control Register for root HA MPAM override registers
F 3 1 cfg_ctl
DESC Secure Control Register for root HA config control registers
R 0x988 64 - ROOT por_ccg_ha_rcr
RESET 0x0 0xf
DESC Root Control Registers for predefined groups of root registers.
F 0 1 ldid_ctl
DESC Root Control Register for root HA LDID registers
F 1 1 linkid_ctl
DESC Root Control Register for root HA Link ID registers
F 2 1 mpam_ctl
DESC Root Control Register for root HA MPAM override registers
F 3 1 cfg_ctl
DESC Root Control Register for root HA config control registers
R 0xa00 64 - ROOT por_ccg_ha_cfg_ctl
RESET 0x640040 0x1ffffff
DESC Functions as the configuration control register. Specifies the current mode.
RGO por_ccg_ha_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_ccg_ha_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 qos_override_en
DESC QoS override en When set, QoS value on CHI side is driven from QoS override value in this register
F 1 4 qos_override
DESC QoS override value
F 5 1 ns_override_en
DESC NS override en When set, NS(Non-Secure) value on CHI side is driven from NS override value in this register
F 6 1 ns_override
DESC NS override value
F 7 1 nse_override_en
DESC NSE override en When set, NSE(Non-Secure) value on CHI side is driven from NSE override value in this register
F 8 1 nse_override
DESC NSE override value
F 9 1 drop_writes_on_cxl_reset
DESC When set, write requests over CCL will be dropped during CXL Reset. Propagate by default
F 10 1 drop_transactions_on_inbound_cxl_viral
DESC When set, write/read requests over CCL will be dropped during Inbound CXL Viral. Propagate by default
F 11 1 ha_txn_timeout_enable
DESC When Set this bit enables CCG HA Transaction Timeout mechanism.
F 12 4 ha_txn_timeout_value
DESC this field allows system software to modify the Transaction Timeout Value for CCG HA Transactions: 4'b0000 : 50us  to 10ms 4'b0001 : 50us  to 100us 4'b0010 : 1ms   to 10ms 4'b0101 : 16ms  to 55ms 4'b0110 : 65ms  to 210ms 4'b1001 : 260ms to 900ms 4'b1010 : 1s    to 3.5s 4'b1101 : 4s    to 13s 4'b1110 : 17s   to 64s others  : Reserved
F 16 4 ha_txn_timeout_threshold
DESC The number of transaction timeouts, which would trigger UE
F 20 1 ha_dsa_mode_en
DESC Enables DSA mode, ReadNoSnp & WriteNoSnp requests are sent to SN
F 21 1 ha_c2c_early_dbid_en
DESC C2C, for 3-hop flows Enables the early-dbid flow
F 22 1 ha_c2c_early_readreceipt_en
DESC C2C, for ordered read requests, HA enables the early-readreceipt flow
F 23 1 ha_c2c_rxdat_qos_prop_en
DESC For C2C, propagate QOS from CHI-DAT port to CHI-C2C. If disabled, QOS=0 on C2C
F 24 1 ha_c2c_txdat_qos_prop_en
DESC For C2C, propagate QOS from CHI-C2C to CHI-DAT port. If disabled, reflect request value
R 0xa08 64 - ROOT por_ccg_ha_aux_ctl
RESET 0x2213c0008 0xfffff006f
DESC Functions as the auxiliary control register for CXHA.
F 0 1 cg_disable
DESC Disables clock gating when set
F 1 1 snoop_dataret_disable
DESC Disables setting data return for CCIX snoop requests for all CHI snoop opcodes
F 2 1 remote_chia_rnf_present
DESC Indicates existence of CHIA RN-F in system; HA uses this indication to send SnpToS or SnpToSC 1'b0: HA converts SnpShared, SnpClean, and SnpNotSharedDirty to SnpToSC 1'b1: HA converts SnpShared, SnpClean, and SnpNotSharedDirty to SnpToS
F 3 1 early_compack_en
DESC Early CompAck enable; enables sending early CompAck on CCIX for requests that require CompAck
F 5 1 disable_cg_flopen
DESC Disables enhanced flop enable control for dynamic power savings
F 6 1 disable_chic_dmt
DESC When set disables CHI-C style DMT
F 16 1 snpreq_copyback_haz_en
DESC When set enables Snoop-CopyBack hazarding at incoming Snoop Request pipe
F 17 1 passive_buf_force_ue
DESC When set, focres all DE's originating in Passive Buffer to be reported as UEs
F 18 2 max_nd_rspout_msgs
DESC Used to configure the maximum number of non-data response messages (Completions/GO/WritePulls) presented to CCLA's packing logic. 2'b00: one message 2'b01: two messages 2'b10: three messages 2'b11: four messages Note: The max is further limited by max allowed by the given protocol (CCIX2.0/CXL.mem/CXL.cache)
F 20 2 max_dat_rspout_msgs
DESC Used to configure the maximum number of response data messages (Read Data) presented to CCLA's packing logic. 2'b00: one message 2'b01: two messages 2'b10: three messages 2'b11: four messages Note: The max is further limited by max allowed by the given protocol (CCIX2.0/CXL.mem/CXL.cache)
F 22 1 cxl_rspvhitv_force_uc
DESC When set, forces UC response state for Snoop response on CHI when D2H RspVHitV response is received on CXL
F 23 1 disable_cxl_hw_snoopdomain_reqack
DESC When set, disables CXL Hardware based Snoop domain handshake
F 24 1 earlycomp_dis
DESC When set, disables sending early completions for requests. This is applicable to CXL.Cache (writebacks that come with Data) - D2H_DIRTYEVICT
F 25 1 cxl_upd_snpcurr2snpdata
DESC When set, updates SnpCurr to SnpData on CXL.Cache
F 26 1 cxl_disable_mem_attr_overriding
DESC When set, Disables the static memory attributes on the CHI reqs and derives from RNSAM configuration based on HTG/non-hashed regions
F 27 1 use_4bit_data_source_enc
DESC When set, forces use of 4-bit Data Source Encoding
F 28 1 use_5bit_data_source_enc
DESC When set, forces use of 5-bit Data Source Encoding (CHI-F)
F 29 1 pass_wlast_on_axid
DESC When set, forces last txn indicator received from remote chip to be passed as the MSB of AWID for CCG_RNI instance (if present)
F 30 1 dct_compdat_loopback_en
DESC When set, enables COMPDATA loopback from HA TXDAT to HA RXDAT. This scenario arises when snoopee and requestor are both in the Remote (HA sends COMPDATA to itself)
F 31 1 downgrade_dct_copyback_haz_en
DESC When set, Downgrades the Forward Snoop opcodes to the non-forward Snoops during the Copyback hazarding scenarios (data is sent to HNF only). When Reset, Data is sent to RN & HN depending on the RetToSrc and the Copyback opcode.
F 32 1 cxl_type1_host_disable_hns_routing
DESC When set, HA bypasses HNS for LBT bound transactions and directly steers LBT bound transactions to RA
F 33 1 cxl_type1_host_disable_hns_routing_for_memwr
DESC When set, HA disable sending CXL memWR transactions(LBT bound) to the LCN. MemWR transactions (LBT bound) are steered to RA.
F 34 1 cxl_type1_host_disable_hns_routing_for_itomwr
DESC When set, HA disable sending CXL ItoMWR transactions(LBT bound) to the LCN. ItoMWR transactions (LBT bound) are steered to RA.
F 35 1 downgrade_dct_en
DESC When set, Downgrades the Forward Snoop opcodes to the non-forward Snoops.
