R 0x1340 32 WO ROOT por_ccla_cxl_dcd_write_intf
RESET 0x0 0xffff7fff
DESC Write Interface to Dynamic Capacity LUT. Only applicable for Device. Host does not use this register
RGO por_ccla_rcr.cxllink_ctl
SGO por_ccla_scr.cxllink_ctl
F 0 15 dcd_lut_write_address
DESC Corresponds to LUT entry to write. Number of entries is limited by CCG_HA_DCD_LUT_DEPTH_PARAM
F 16 15 dcd_lut_write_data
DESC Data that will be written to the LUT. Based on number of entries in the region being accessed, any unused most significant bits for this field must be set to zero
F 31 1 dcd_lut_entry_valid
DESC LUT Entry valid. Set this bit to indicate that the LUT entry is now ready to use. Clear this bit to invalidate LUT entry
R 0x1348 32 - ROOT por_ccla_cxl_dcd_read_intf
RESET 0x0 0xffff7fff
DESC Read Interface to Dynamic Capacity LUT. Only applicable for Device. Host does not use this register. To read LUT entry, first write to this register to program the read address. A subsequent read to this register will then return the data read from the LUT
RGO por_ccla_rcr.cxllink_ctl
SGO por_ccla_scr.cxllink_ctl
F 0 15 dcd_lut_read_address
DESC Corresponds to LUT entry to read. Number of entries is limited by CCG_HA_DCD_LUT_DEPTH_PARAM. On reads, returns the last address programmed in this field. Returns zero in Host mode
F 16 15 dcd_lut_read_data
DESC Data read from the LUT. Data is loaded from LUT and will be valid after a write is performed to program the read address. Returns zero in Host mode
F 31 1 dcd_lut_entry_valid
DESC LUT Entry status
R 0x1458 64 V ROOT por_ccla_ull_idle_counter
RESET 0x20 0xffff
DESC The number of cycles ull needs to be down for it to be counted as idle
F 0 16 ull_counter
DESC ull counter
R 0x1500 64 - ROOT por_ccla_ide_freq_factor
RESET 0x0 0x3
DESC Register contents are used as ratio of freq between Host and device.
RGO por_ccla_rcr.cxllink_ctl
SGO por_ccla_scr.cxllink_ctl
F 0 2 freq_factor
DESC Freq factor encodings. This field is used by ULL to determine the number of cycles it has to wait during the IDE key programming stage or after sending IDE TMAC to start a new MAC epoch. For example: If CMN(ULL) is running at 2GHz and LLL is running at 1GHZ, select freq factor 2'b01 which gives a 1:2 ratio. This freq factor determines the number of cycles based on the number of flits programmed either in key_refresh or truncation transmit delay registers. 2'b00 - 1:1 2'b01 - 1:2 2'b10 - 1:3 2'b11 - 1:4
R 0x1bf8 64 - ROOT por_ccg_multi_mesh_chn_ctrl
RESET 0x0 0x1
DESC Valid when two CHI TX response channels are enabled. Functions as the control register for Target based channel selection in Multi-Mesh Channel structure.
RGO por_ccla_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_ccla_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 multi_mesh_chn_sel_programmed
DESC Indicates that multi CHI VC channel configured for all the targets specified in the channel select registers.
R 0x1c08 64 - ROOT por_ccg_multi_mesh_chn_sel_0
RESET 0x0 0xbfff3fff3fff3fff
DESC Valid when two CHI TX response channels are enabled. Functions as the CHI VC channel select per Target register in Multi-Mesh Channel structure. The register holds the target Ids for overriding the default channel selection and the response port to be used
RGO por_ccla_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_ccla_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 mesh_channel_sel_0
DESC CHI VC channel select: 1 - CHI VC channel 1 is selected, 0 - CHI VC channel 0 is selected
F 1 11 tgtid_0
DESC 11-bit Target ID associated with the corresponding channel_sel field. This field is used in the LUP to determine which CHI VC channel the FLIT has to be routed to for this target.
F 12 2 cal_dev_chn_map_sel_0
DESC Channel Map select for target devices behind CAL (associated with the corresponding tgtid field): 2'b00: CAL2: All devices behind CAL are mapped to same channel in the Multi-Channel Mesh structure as specified below (applicable for Mesh with > 2 device ports per XP), - CAL2: DEV0,DEV1 are mapped to same channel, 2'b01: CAL4: All devices behind CAL are mapped to same channel in the Multi-Channel Mesh structure as specified below, - CAL4: DEV0,DEV1,DEV2,DEV3 are mapped to same channel, 2'b10: Reserved, 2'b11: Each target device behind CAL can be mapped to different channel in the Multi-Channel Mesh structure as specified below, - CAL2: DEV0,DEV1 can be mapped to different channel, - CAL4: DEV0,DEV1,DEV2,DEV3 can be mapped to different channel
F 16 1 mesh_channel_sel_1
DESC CHI VC channel select: 1 - CHI VC channel 1 is selected, 0 - CHI VC channel 0 is selected
F 17 11 tgtid_1
