DESC por_ccla_errmisc_NS<01> valid 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 2 ce W1C
DESC Corrected errors 2'b10: At least one corrected error recorded 2'b00: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 de W1C
DESC Deferred errors 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
F 22 1 pn W1C
DESC Poison 1'b1: Uncorrected error recorded because a poison value was consumed 1'b0: Other cases
F 20 2 uet W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error Type, valid only when UE != 0 2'b01: Uncorrected error, Unrecoverable error (UEU). 2'b00: Invalid
F 8 8 ierr W1C
DESC Implementation-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: Partner implementation defined error
F 0 8 serr W1C
DESC 8'h00: No error 8'h01: IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED error - refer to por_ccla_errmisc1.ERRSRC 8'h02: Data value from (non-associative) internal memory. For example, Error Correction Code (ECC) from on-chip SRAM or buffer. 8'h12: Error response from Completer of access. For example, error response from cache write-back. 8'h13: External timeout. For example, timeout on interaction with another component. 8'h17 or 8'h18: Deferred error from Completer/Requester passed through. For example, poisoned data received from the Completer/Requester of an access and returned to the Requester. 
