R 0xd900 64 - - por_hni_pmu_event_sel
RESET 0x0 0x3f3f3f3f
DESC Specifies the PMU event to be counted.
F 0 6 pmu_event0_id
DESC HN-I PMU Event 0 select 6'h00: No event 6'h20: RRT read occupancy count overflow 6'h21: RRT write occupancy count overflow 6'h22: RDT read occupancy count overflow 6'h23: RDT write occupancy count overflow 6'h24: WDB occupancy count overflow 6'h25: RRT read allocation 6'h26: RRT write allocation 6'h27: RDT read allocation 6'h28: RDT write allocation 6'h29: WDB allocation 6'h2A: RETRYACK TXRSP flit sent 6'h2B: ARVALID set without ARREADY event 6'h2C: ARREADY set without ARVALID event 6'h2D: AWVALID set without AWREADY event 6'h2E: AWREADY set without AWVALID event 6'h2F: WVALID set without WREADY event 6'h30: TXDAT stall (TXDAT valid but no link credit available) 6'h31: Non-PCIe serialization event 6'h32: PCIe serialization event NOTE: All other encodings are reserved.
F 8 6 pmu_event1_id
DESC HN-I PMU Event 1 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 16 6 pmu_event2_id
DESC HN-I PMU Event 2 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 24 6 pmu_event3_id
DESC HN-I PMU Event 3 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
R 0xd908 64 - - por_hnp_pmu_event_sel
RESET 0x0 0x3f3f3f3f
DESC Specifies the PMU event to be counted. HNP only
F 0 6 pmu_event0_id
DESC P2P/ADW Slice PMU Event 0 select 6'h00: No event 6'h01: P2P Write Slice RRT write occupancy count overflow 6'h02: P2P Write Slice RDT write occupancy count overflow 6'h03: P2P Write Slice WDB occupancy count overflow 6'h04: P2P Write Slice RRT write allocation 6'h05: P2P Write Slice RDT write allocation 6'h06: P2P Write Slice WDB allocation 6'h07: P2P Write Slice AWVALID set without AWREADY event 6'h08: P2P Write Slice AWREADY set without AWVALID event 6'h09: P2P Write Slice WVALID set without WREADY event 6'h11: P2P Read Slice RRT read occupancy count overflow 6'h12: P2P Read Slice RDT read occupancy count overflow 6'h13: P2P Read Slice RRT read allocation 6'h14: P2P Read Slice RDT read allocation 6'h15: P2P Read Slice ARVALID set without ARREADY event 6'h16: P2P Read Slice ARREADY set without ARVALID event 6'h21: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice RRT write occupancy count overflow 6'h22: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice RDT write occupancy count overflow 6'h23: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice WDB occupancy count overflow 6'h24: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice RRT write allocation 6'h25: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice RDT write allocation 6'h26: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice WDB allocation 6'h27: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice AWVALID set without AWREADY event 6'h28: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice AWREADY set without AWVALID event 6'h29: Atomic/Deferrable Write Slice WVALID set without WREADY event NOTE: All other encodings are reserved.
F 8 6 pmu_event1_id
DESC P2P/ADW Slice PMU Event 1 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 16 6 pmu_event2_id
DESC P2P/ADW Slice PMU Event 2 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 24 6 pmu_event3_id
DESC P2P/ADW Slice PMU Event 3 select; see pmu_event0_id for encodings"
R 0xe000 64 RO ROOT por_hni_errfr
RESET 0x120000801201a2 0x720000803ffff3
DESC Error Feature Register for Root
RGO por_hni_rcr.ras
SGO por_hni_scr.ras
F 0 2 ed
DESC Error reporting and logging 2'b10: Error reporting and logging is controllable using por_hni_errctlr.ED
F 4 2 ui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt for Uncorrected Errors 2'b10: Error handling interrupt is supported and controllable using por_hni_errctlr.UI
F 6 2 fi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt 2'b10: Fault handling interrupt is supported and controllable using por_hni_errctlr.FI
F 8 2 ue
DESC In-band error response 2'b01: In-band error response (External Abort) is supported and always enabled
F 10 2 cfi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt for Corrected Errors control 2'b00: Does not support the control for enabling fault handling interrupts on corrected errors
F 12 3 cec
DESC Corrected Error Counter 3'b000: Does not implement the standard Corrected error counter model
F 15 1 rp
DESC Repeat Corrected Error Counter 1'b0: Reserved, RES0
F 16 2 dui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt for Deferred Errors control 2'b10: Control for enabling error recovery interrupts on deferred errors is supported and controlled using por_hni_errctlr.DUI
F 18 2 ceo
DESC Corrected Error Overwrite 2'b00: Reserved, RES0
F 20 2 inj
DESC Fault Injection Extension 2'b01: The node implements the RAS Common Fault Injection Model Extension
F 31 1 frx
DESC Feature Register Extension 1'b1: por_hni_errfr[63:48] are defined by the architecture
F 49 1 ueu
DESC Unrecoverable Error recording 1'b1: Unrecoverable Error supported
F 52 1 de
DESC Deferred Error recording 1'b1: Deffered Error supported
F 53 2 ce
DESC Corrected Error recording 2'b00: Corrected Error not supported
R 0xe008 64 - ROOT por_hni_errctlr
RESET 0x0 0x50d
DESC Error Control Register for Root
RGO por_hni_rcr.ras
SGO por_hni_scr.ras
F 0 1 ed
DESC Error reporting and logging enable
F 2 1 ui
DESC Uncorrected error recovery interrupt enable
F 3 1 fi
DESC Fault handling interrupt enable
F 8 1 cfi
DESC Fault handling interrupt for Corrected Errors enable
F 10 1 dui
DESC Error recovery interrupt for Deferred Errors enable
R 0xe010 64 - ROOT por_hni_errstatus
RESET 0x0 0xfff0ffff
DESC Error Status Register for Root
RGO por_hni_rcr.ras
SGO por_hni_scr.ras
F 0 8 serr W1C
DESC Architecturally-defined primary error code 8'h00: No error 8'h01: IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED error.  Refer to por_hni_errmisc1.ERRSRC for error type details.
F 8 8 ierr W1C
DESC Implementation-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: Partner implementation defined error
F 20 2 uet W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error Type 2'b00: Invalid 2'b01: Uncorrected error, Unrecoverable error (UEU).
F 22 1 pn W1C
DESC Poison 1'b0: Uncorrected or Deferred error recorded because a corrupt value was detected 1'b1: Uncorrected or Deferred error recorded because a poison value was detected
F 23 1 de W1C
DESC Deferred Error 1'b0: No errors were deferred 1'b1: At least one error was not corrected and is deferred
F 24 2 ce W1C
DESC Corrected Error 2'b00: No errors were corrected
F 26 1 mv W1C
DESC Miscellaneous Register Valid 1'b0: por_hni_errmisc register not valid 1'b1: por_hni_errmisc register contains additional information for an error recorded by this node
F 27 1 of W1C
DESC Overflow 1'b0: Since last cleared to zero, no error syndrome has been discarded 1'b1: Since last cleared to zero, at least one error syndrome has been discarded
F 28 1 er W1C
DESC Error Reported 1'b0: No in-band error response signaled 1'b1: In-band error response was signaled to the Requester
F 29 1 ue W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected 1'b1: At least one detected error was not corrected and not deferred
F 30 1 v W1C
DESC Status Register Valid 1'b0: por_hni_errstatus not valid 1'b1: por_hni_errstatus valid. At least one error has been recorded
F 31 1 av W1C
DESC Address Valid 1'b0: por_hni_erraddr not valid 1'b1: por_hni_erraddr contains an address associated with the highest priority error recorded by this node
R 0xe018 64 - ROOT por_hni_erraddr
RESET 0x0 0xc80fffffffffffff
DESC Error Address Register for Root NOTE: BRESP and poison errors (0x8-0xA in por_hni_errmisc1.ERRSRC) do not record anything in por_hni_erraddr.
RGO por_hni_rcr.ras
SGO por_hni_scr.ras
F 0 52 paddr
DESC Physical Address
F 59 1 nse
DESC Non-Secure Extension attribute (NSE, also PAS[1])
F 62 1 si
DESC PAS Incorrect 1'b0: PAS[1:0] is correct 1'b1: PAS[1:0] might not be correct
F 63 1 ns
DESC Non-Secure attribute (NS, also PAS[0])
R 0xe020 64 - ROOT por_hni_errmisc1
RESET 0x0 0x1f300007f7f7fff
DESC Error Miscellaneous Register 1
RGO por_hni_rcr.ras
SGO por_hni_scr.ras
F 0 4 errsrc
DESC Error source 4'b0000: Coherent read 4'b0001: Coherent write 4'b0010: Coherent dataless (CleanUnique/MakeUnique/Evict/StashOnce/CMO) 4'b0011: Atomic 4'b0100: Illegal configuration read 4'b0101: Illegal configuration write or dataless 4'b0110: Configuration write data partial byte enable error 4'b0111: Configuration write data parity error or poison error 4'b1000: BRESP error 4'b1001: Poison error 4'b1010: BRESP error and poison error 4'b1011: Unsupported Exclusive access (HN-P only) NOTE: BRESP and poison errors (0x8-0xA) are Uncorrectable Errors (UE). SRCID and ERRSRC are the only valid fields in por_hni_errmisc1. All other error types are Deferred Errors (DE) and all fields are valid.
F 4 11 srcid
DESC CHI Source ID field
F 16 7 opcode
DESC CHI Opcode field
F 24 4 memattr
DESC CHI Memory Attributes field
F 28 3 size
DESC CHI Size field
F 48 2 order
DESC CHI Order field
F 52 5 lpid
DESC CHI Logic Processor ID (LPID) field
