RESET 0x0 0x1fff00000003000f
DESC Functions as the Root PAS miscellaneous error register 1. Contains additional information about errors.
RGO por_mtu_rcr.ras
SGO por_mtu_scr.ras
F 0 4 errsrc
DESC Error source 4'b0001: Data single-bit ECC 4'b0010: Data double-bit ECC 4'b0011: Single-bit ECC overflow 4'b0101: Control single-bit ECC 4'b0110: Control double-bit ECC 4'b1000: AXI AR Subordinate Error 4'b1001: AXI AR Decode Error 4'b1010: AXI AR Poison Error 4'b1011: AXI AR Datachk Error 4'b1100: AXI W Subordinate Error 4'b1101: AXI W Decode Error 4'b1110: PA out of range Error
F 16 2 optype
DESC Error opcode type 2'b00: Read Type (RD_NO_SNP, PrefetchTgt) 2'b01: Write (WR_NO_SNP) 2'b10: CMO, WR+CMO 2'b11: Other
F 48 13 errset
DESC TC set address for ECC Single bit error
R 0xe030 64 - ROOT por_mtu_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x7fffffffffffff
DESC Enables error injection and setup. When enabled for a given PA and PAS (NSE/NS), MTU returns an error interrupt which emulates a TC double-bit data ECC error. This feature enables software to test the error handler. The error is reported for cacheable read access with Tag Op Transfer for which TC hit. No error is reported for cacheable read access for which TC miss.
