R 0xa70 64 - ROOT por_mxp_device_port_disable
RESET 0xffffffff 0xffffffff
DESC Controls whether a device port attached to the SMXP is disabled
F 0 4 p0_device_disable
DESC Port 0 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 4 4 p1_device_disable
DESC Port 1 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 8 4 p2_device_disable
DESC Port 2 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 12 4 p3_device_disable
DESC Port 3 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 16 4 p4_device_disable
DESC Port 4 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 20 4 p5_device_disable
DESC Port 5 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 24 4 p6_device_disable
DESC Port 5 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
F 28 4 p7_device_disable
DESC Port 5 device disabled 4'b0001: Disable device 0 4'b0010: Disable device 1 4'b0100: Disable device 2 4'b1000: Disable device 3
R 0xa78 64 - ROOT por_mxp_cfg_ctl
RESET 0x0 0x7
DESC Functions as the configuration control register for MXP.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_mxp_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 dsa_en
DESC Enables Direct Subordinate Access feature to SBSX/MTSX. Requires POR_DSA_EN_PARAM to be set, otherwise this config bit has no effect.
F 1 1 ifc_err_disable
DESC Disable FUSA IFC ERR generation in MXP
F 2 1 e2e_err_disable
DESC Disable FUSA IFC ERR generation in MXP
R 0xa80 64 - ROOT por_mxp_p0_qos_control
RESET 0x0 0xf0055
DESC Controls QoS settings for devices connected to port 0.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.qos
SGO por_mxp_scr.qos
F 0 1 p0_lat_en
DESC Enables port 0 QoS regulation when set
F 2 1 p0_qos_override_en
DESC Enables port 0 QoS override; when set, allows QoS value on inbound transactions to be overridden
F 4 1 p0_reg_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode 1'b0: Latency mode 1'b1: Period mode; used for bandwidth regulation
F 6 1 p0_pqv_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode during period mode 1'b0: Normal mode; QoS value is stable when the manager is idle 1'b1: Quiesce high mode; QoS value tends to the maximum value when the manager is idle
F 16 4 p0_qos_override
DESC QoS override value for port 0
R 0xa88 64 - ROOT por_mxp_p0_qos_lat_tgt
RESET 0x0 0xfff
DESC Controls QoS target latency/period (in cycles) for regulation of devices connected to port 0.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.qos
SGO por_mxp_scr.qos
F 0 12 p0_lat_tgt
DESC Port 0 transaction target latency/period; a value of 0 corresponds to no regulation
R 0xa90 64 - ROOT por_mxp_p0_qos_lat_scale
RESET 0x0 0x7
DESC Controls the QoS target scale factor for devices connected to port 0. The scale factor is represented in powers of two from the range 2^(-3) to 2^(-10).
RGO por_mxp_rcr.qos
SGO por_mxp_scr.qos
F 0 3 p0_lat_scale
DESC Port 0 QoS scale factor 3'b000: 2^(-3) 3'b001: 2^(-4) 3'b010: 2^(-5) 3'b011: 2^(-6) 3'b100: 2^(-7) 3'b101: 2^(-8) 3'b110: 2^(-9) 3'b111: 2^(-10)
R 0xa98 64 - ROOT por_mxp_p0_qos_lat_range
RESET 0x0 0xf0f
DESC Controls the minimum and maximum QoS values generated by the QoS regulator for devices connected to port 0.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.qos
SGO por_mxp_scr.qos
F 0 4 p0_lat_min_qos
DESC Port 0 QoS minimum value
F 8 4 p0_lat_max_qos
DESC Port 0 QoS maximum value
