R 0xe000 64 RO ROOT por_mxp_errfr
RESET 0x120000801201a2 0x720000803ffff3
DESC Functions as the error feature register.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO por_mxp_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 0 2 ed
DESC Error reporting and logging control 2'b10: Error reporting and logging is controllable using por_mxp_errctlr.ED
F 4 2 ui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt on Uncorrected errors and controllable using por_mxp_errctlr.UI.
F 6 2 fi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Deferred and Uncorrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on Deferred and Uncorrected errors and controllable using por_mxp_errctlr.FI.
F 8 2 ue
DESC In-band error response is always on
F 10 2 cfi
DESC Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors control 2'b00: Does not support Fault Handling Interrupt from Corrected errors 2'b10: Support Fault Handling Interrupt on corrected errors and controllable using por_mxp_errctlr.CFI.
F 12 3 cec
DESC Standard corrected error counter 3'b000: Does not implement standard error counter model 3'b100: Implements a 16-bit Corrected error counter in por_mxp_errmisc0
F 15 1 rp
DESC Repeat counter (valid only when por_mxp_errfr.CEC != 3'b000.) 1'b0: Invalid; 1'b1: Implements a first (repeat) counter and a second (other) counter in por_mxp_errmisc0
F 16 2 dui
DESC Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors control 2'b00: Does not support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors 2'b10: Support Error Recovery Interrupt from Deferred errors and controllable using por_mxp_errctlr.DUI.
F 18 2 ceo
DESC Corrected Error overwrite. 2'b00: Keep the first Corrected Error syndrome
F 20 2 inj
DESC Fault Injection Extension. 2'b01: Support Common Fault Injection Model Extension
F 31 1 frx
DESC Feature Register extension. 1'b1: por_mxp_errfr[63:48] is architecturally defined
F 49 1 ueu
DESC Unrecoverable Error recording 1'b0: Unrecoverable Error not supported 1'b1: Unrecoverable Error supported
F 52 1 de
DESC Deferred Error recording 1'b0: Deferred Error not supported 1'b1: Deffered Error supported
F 53 2 ce
DESC Corrected Error recording 2'b00: Corrected Error not supported 2'b10: Non-specific Corrected Error supported
R 0xe008 64 - ROOT por_mxp_errctlr
RESET 0x0 0x50d
DESC Functions as the error control register. Controls whether specific error-handling interrupts and error detection/deferment are enabled.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO por_mxp_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 0 1 ed
DESC Enables error detection as specified in por_mxp_errfr.ED
F 2 1 ui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for uncorrected error as specified in por_mxp_errfr.UI
F 3 1 fi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for uncorrected and deferred errors as specified in por_mxp_errfr.FI
F 8 1 cfi
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for corrected error as specified in por_mxp_errfr.CFI
F 10 1 dui
DESC Enables error recovery interrupt for deferred error as specified in por_mxp_errfr.DUI
R 0xe010 64 - ROOT por_mxp_errstatus
RESET 0x0 0xfff0ffff
DESC Functions as the error status register. AV and MV bits must be cleared in the same cycle, otherwise the error record does not have a consistent view.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO por_mxp_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 31 1 av W1C
DESC Address register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Address is valid 1'b0: Address is not valid
F 30 1 v W1C
DESC Register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error recorded; register is valid 1'b0: No errors recorded
F 29 1 ue W1C
DESC Uncorrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error detected that is not corrected and is not deferred to a subordinate 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected
F 28 1 er W1C
DESC Error Reported 1'b1: In-band error response signaled to the Requester 1'b0: No in-band error response signaled
F 27 1 of W1C
DESC Overflow; asserted when multiple errors of the highest priority type are detected; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: More than one error detected 1'b0: None or only one error detected as described by UE/DE/CE fields
F 26 1 mv W1C
DESC por_mxp_errmisc valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 2 ce W1C
DESC Corrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 2'b10: At least one corrected error recorded 2'b00: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 de W1C
DESC Deferred errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
F 22 1 pn W1C
DESC Poison 1'b1: Uncorrected error recorded because a poison value was consumed 1'b0: Other cases
F 20 2 uet W1C
DESC Uncorrected Error Type, valid only when UE != 0 2'b01: Uncorrected error, Unrecoverable error (UEU). 2'b00: Invalid
F 8 8 ierr W1C
DESC Implementation-defined primary error code. bit 0: Partner implementation defined error bit 1: FUSA IFC_ERR error bit 2: FUSA E2E_ERR error other bits: reserved
F 0 8 serr W1C
DESC Architecturally-defined primary error code. 8'h00: No error 8'h01: IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED error.  Refer to por_mxp_errmisc1.ERRSRC for error type details.
R 0xe018 64 - ROOT por_mxp_erraddr
RESET 0x0 0xc80fffffffffffff
DESC Contains the error record address.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO por_mxp_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 0 52 addr
DESC Transaction address
F 59 1 nse
DESC Root status of transaction.  PAS[1] of the transaction.
F 62 1 si
DESC {NSE,NS} valid 1'b0: PAS field is valid 1'b1: PAS field is invalid
F 63 1 ns
DESC Security status of transaction.  PAS[0] of the transaction.
R 0xe028 64 - ROOT por_mxp_errmisc1
RESET 0x0 0x87ff0077007fffff
DESC Functions as the miscellaneous error register. Contains miscellaneous information about deferred/uncorrected errors.
RGO por_mxp_rcr.ras_secure_access_override
SGO por_mxp_scr.ras_secure_access_override
F 63 1 tlpmsg
DESC Error flit TLPMSG Status
F 48 11 tgtid
DESC Error flit target ID
F 36 3 fusa_err_dev
DESC FUSA error device
F 32 3 fusa_err_port
DESC FUSA error port
F 16 7 opcode
DESC Error flit opcode
F 5 11 srcid
DESC Error flit source ID
F 0 5 errsrc
DESC Error source for Mesh With 8 ports: Bits [3:2]: Transaction type 2'b00: REQ 2'b01: RSP 2'b10: SNP 2'b11: DAT Bits [4,1:0]: Port 3'b000:  Port 0 3'b001:  Port 1 3'b010:  Port 2 3'b011:  Port 3 3'b100:  Port 4 3'b101:  Port 5 3'b110:  Port 6 3'b111:  Port 7
Mesh With Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: REQ2 3'b101: RSP2 3'b110: SNP2 3'b111: DAT2 Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh Without Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: Reserved 3'b101: Reserved 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh With Single MXP (1x1 Mesh): Bits [4:3]: Transaction type 2'b00:  REQ 2'b01:  RSP 2'b10:  SNP 2'b11:  DAT Bits [2:0]: Port 3'b000: Port 0 3'b001: Port 1 3'b010: Port 2 3'b011: Port 3 3'b100: Port 4 3'b101: Port 5
