DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for write transactions during period mode 1'b0: Normal mode; QoS value is stable when the manager is idle 1'b1: Quiesce high mode; QoS value tends to the maximum value when the manager is idle
F 7 1 s2_ar_pqv_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for read transactions during period mode 1'b0: Normal mode; QoS value is stable when the manager is idle 1'b1: Quiesce high mode; QoS value tends to the maximum value when the manager is idle
F 16 4 s2_aw_qos_override
DESC AW QoS override value for port S2
F 20 4 s2_ar_qos_override
DESC AR QoS override value for port S2
R 0xac8 64 - ROOT por_rnd_s2_qos_lat_tgt
RESET 0x0 0xfff0fff
DESC Controls QoS target latency (in cycles) for regulations of port S2 read and write transactions.
RGO por_rnd_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rnd_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 12 s2_aw_lat_tgt
DESC Port S2 AW channel target latency; a value of 0 corresponds to no regulation
F 16 12 s2_ar_lat_tgt
DESC Port S2 AR channel target latency; a value of 0 corresponds to no regulation
R 0xad0 64 - ROOT por_rnd_s2_qos_lat_scale
RESET 0x0 0x707
DESC Controls the QoS target latency scale factor for port S2 read and write transactions. This register represents powers of two from the range 2^(-5) to 2^(-12); it is used to match a 16-bit integrator.
RGO por_rnd_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rnd_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 3 s2_aw_lat_scale
DESC Port S2 AW QoS scale factor 3'b000: 2^(-5) 3'b001: 2^(-6) 3'b010: 2^(-7) 3'b011: 2^(-8) 3'b100: 2^(-9) 3'b101: 2^(-10) 3'b110: 2^(-11) 3'b111: 2^(-12)
F 8 3 s2_ar_lat_scale
DESC Port S2 AR QoS scale factor 3'b000: 2^(-5) 3'b001: 2^(-6) 3'b010: 2^(-7) 3'b011: 2^(-8) 3'b100: 2^(-9) 3'b101: 2^(-10) 3'b110: 2^(-11) 3'b111: 2^(-12)
R 0xad8 64 - ROOT por_rnd_s2_qos_lat_range
RESET 0x0 0xf0f0f0f
DESC Controls the minimum and maximum QoS values generated by the QoS latency regulator for port S2 read and write transactions.
RGO por_rnd_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rnd_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 4 s2_aw_lat_min_qos
DESC Port S2 AW QoS minimum value
F 8 4 s2_aw_lat_max_qos
DESC Port S2 AW QoS maximum value
F 16 4 s2_ar_lat_min_qos
DESC Port S2 AR QoS minimum value
F 24 4 s2_ar_lat_max_qos
DESC Port S2 AR QoS maximum value
R 0x1900 64 V ROOT por_rnd_syscoreq_ctl
RESET 0x0 0x7
DESC Functions as the RN-D DVM domain control register. Provides a software alternative to hardware SYSCOREQ/SYSCOACK handshake. Works with por_rnd_syscoack_status.
F 0 1 s0_dvmdomain_req
DESC Controls DVM domain enable (SYSCOREQ) for port S0
F 1 1 s1_dvmdomain_req
DESC Controls DVM domain enable (SYSCOREQ) for port S1
F 2 1 s2_dvmdomain_req
DESC Controls DVM domain enable (SYSCOREQ) for port S2
R 0x1908 64 ROV ROOT por_rnd_syscoack_status
RESET 0x0 0x7
DESC Functions as the RN-D DVM domain status register. Provides a software alternative to hardware SYSCOREQ/SYSCOACK handshake. Works with por_rnd_syscoreq_ctl.
F 0 1 s0_dvmdomain_ack
DESC Provides DVM domain status (SYSCOACK) for port S0
F 1 1 s1_dvmdomain_ack
DESC Provides DVM domain status (SYSCOACK) for port S1
F 2 1 s2_dvmdomain_ack
DESC Provides DVM domain status (SYSCOACK) for port S2
R 0xd900 64 - - por_rnd_pmu_event_sel
RESET 0x0 0x7f7f7f7f
DESC Specifies the PMU event to be counted.
F 0 7 pmu_event0_id
DESC RN-D PMU Event 0 ID 7'h00: No event 7'h01: Port S0 RDataBeats 7'h02: Port S1 RDataBeats 7'h03: Port S2 RDataBeats 7'h04: RXDAT flits received 7'h05: TXDAT flits sent 7'h06: Total TXREQ flits sent 7'h07: Retried TXREQ flits sent 7'h08: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice0 7'h09: WRT occupancy count overflow 7'h0A: Replayed TXREQ flits 7'h0B: WriteCancel sent 7'h0C: Port S0 WDataBeats 7'h0D: Port S1 WDataBeats 7'h0E: Port S2 WDataBeats 7'h0F: RRT allocation 7'h10: WRT allocation 7'h11: PADB occupancy count overflow 7'h12: RPDB occupancy count overflow 7'h13: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice1 7'h14: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice2 7'h15: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice3 7'h16: WRT request throttled 7'h17: RNI backpressure CHI LDB full 7'h18: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice0 7'h19: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice1 7'h1A: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice2 7'h1B: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice3 7'h1C: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice0 7'h1D: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice1 7'h1E: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice2 7'h1F: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice3 7'h20: RRT PCIe RD burst allocation 7'h21: Compressed AWID ordering 7'h22: Atomic data buffer allocation 7'h23: Atomic data buffer occupancy 7'h24: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice4 7'h25: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice5 7'h26: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice6 7'h27: RRT occupancy count overflow_slice7 7'h28: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice4 7'h29: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice5 7'h2A: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice6 7'h2B: RRT normal rd req occupancy count overflow_slice7 7'h2C: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice4 7'h2D: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice5 7'h2E: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice6 7'h2F: RRT PCIe RD burst req occupancy count overflow_slice7 7'h30: RRT CBUSY throttled 7'h31: RRT CBUSY 3 7'h32: RRT CBUSY 2 7'h33: RRT CBUSY 1 7'h34: RRT CBUSY 0 7'h35: WRT CBUSY throttled 7'h36: WRT CBUSY 3 7'h37: WRT CBUSY 2 7'h38: WRT CBUSY 1 7'h39: WRT CBUSY 0 7'h3A: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice0 7'h3B: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice1 7'h3C: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice2 7'h3D: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice3 7'h3E: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice4 7'h3F: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice5 7'h40: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice6 7'h41: RRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow_slice7 7'h42: WRT TXREQ dispatched occupancy count overflow
F 8 7 pmu_event1_id
DESC RN-D PMU Event 1 ID; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 16 7 pmu_event2_id
DESC RN-D PMU Event 2 ID; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
F 24 7 pmu_event3_id
DESC RN-D PMU Event 3 ID; see pmu_event0_id for encodings
ENDGROUP
GROUP por_rni_registers
R 0x0 64 RO - por_rni_node_info
RESET 0xa 0xffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information.
F 0 16 node_type
DESC CMN node type identifier
F 16 16 node_id
DESC Component node ID
PAR NODEID_PARAM
F 32 16 logical_id
DESC Component logical ID
PAR LOGICALID_PARAM
R 0x80 64 RO - por_rni_child_info
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Provides component child identification information.
F 0 16 child_count
DESC Number of child nodes; used in discovery process
F 16 16 child_ptr_offset
DESC Starting register offset which contains pointers to the child nodes
R 0x900 64 RO - por_rni_unit_info
RESET 0x80012001808020 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information for RN-I.
F 0 10 num_wr_reqs
DESC Number of outstanding write requests
PAR RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM
F 10 10 num_rd_reqs
DESC Number of outstanding read requests
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM
F 20 10 num_rd_bufs
DESC Number of read data buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_BUF_PARAM
F 30 10 ax_data_width
DESC AXI interface data width in bits
PAR RNID_AXDATA_WIDTH_PARAM
F 40 1 ax_datapoison_en
DESC Data Poison enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXDATAPOISON_EN_PARAM
F 41 1 force_rdb_prealloc
DESC Force read data buffer preallocation 1'b1: yes 1'b0: no
PAR RNID_FORCE_RDB_PREALLOC_PARAM
F 42 2 a4s_num
DESC Number of AXI4Stream interfaces present
PAR RNI_A4S_NUM_PARAM
F 44 10 a4s_logicalid_base
DESC AXI4Stream interfaces logical ID base
PAR RNI_A4S_LOGICALID_BASE_PARAM
F 54 10 num_atomic_bufs
DESC Number of atomic data buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_ATOMIC_BUF_PARAM
R 0x908 64 RO - por_rni_unit_info2
RESET 0x1a2000020b 0x1fffffffff
DESC Provides additonal component identification information for RN-I.
F 0 6 id_width
DESC AXI ID width for ACE-Lite subordinate ports
PAR RNID_ID_WIDTH_PARAM
F 6 6 num_prealloc_bufs
DESC Number of Pre-allocated Read Data Buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_PREALLOC_BUF_PARAM
F 12 1 pab_en
DESC PUB AUB bridge enable 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNI_PAB_EN_PARAM
F 13 8 pab_logicalid
DESC PUB AUB bridge Logical ID
PAR PAB_LOGICALID_PARAM
F 21 1 ax_loopback_en
DESC LoopBack enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXLOOPBACK_EN_PARAM
F 22 1 ax_mpam_en
DESC MPAM enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXMPAM_EN_PARAM
F 23 10 num_rd_req_max_per_slice
DESC Number of read request entires per slice
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_MAX_PER_SLICE_PARAM
F 33 1 legacy_decoup_rd
DESC Legacy decoupled read mode, no read burst propagation
PAR RNID_LEGACY_DECOUP_RD_PARAM
F 34 1 ax_mecid_en
DESC MECID enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXMECID_EN_PARAM
F 35 2 ax_num_port
DESC Number of ACE-Lite/AXI4 interfaces present
PAR RNID_NUM_AXI_PORTS_PARAM
R 0x980 64 - ROOT por_rni_rcr
RESET 0x0 0xf
DESC Root register access override.
F 0 1 cfg_ctl
DESC Allows Root override of the configuration control register
F 1 1 port_ctrl
DESC Allows Root override of the AXI port control registers
F 2 1 mpam_ctrl
DESC Allows Root override of the AXI port MPAM override register
F 3 1 qos_ctrl
DESC Allows Root override of the QoS control registers
R 0x988 64 - S por_rni_scr
RESET 0x0 0xf
DESC Secure register access override.
F 0 1 cfg_ctl
DESC Allows Secure override of the configuration control register
F 1 1 port_ctrl
DESC Allows Secure override of the AXI port control registers
F 2 1 mpam_ctrl
DESC Allows Secure override of the AXI port MPAM override register
F 3 1 qos_ctrl
DESC Allows Secure override of the QoS control registers
R 0xa00 64 - ROOT por_rni_cfg_ctl
RESET 0xd000200201c41 0x1ff87ff3ffffff
DESC Functions as the configuration control register. Specifies the current mode.
RGO por_rni_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_rni_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 qpc_en
DESC When set, enables QPC-based scheduling using two QoS priority classes (QoS15 and non-QoS15)
F 1 1 wfc
DESC When set, enables waiting for completion (COMP) before dispatching dependent transaction (TXN)
F 2 1 dis_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes when set
F 3 1 force_prealloc_rdb
DESC When set, all reads from the RN-I are sent with a preallocated read data buffer
PAR RNID_FORCE_RDB_PREALLOC_PARAM
F 4 1 qpc15_entry_rsv_en
DESC Enables QPC15 entry reservation 1'b1: Reserves tracker entry for QoS15 requests 1'b0: Does not reserve tracker entry for QoS15 requests NOTE: Only valid and applicable when por_rni_qpc_en is set
F 5 1 pcie_mstr_present
DESC Indicates PCIe requester/manager is present; must be set if PCIe requester/manager is present upstream of RN-I or RN-D
F 6 1 dis_port_token
DESC If set, disables per port reservation in the tracker(rd and wr)
F 7 1 dis_tunneled_req_throttling
DESC Disables retry based throttling of tunneled write requests
F 8 3 rrt_crdgnt_weight
DESC Determines weight of credit grant allocated to retried reads in presence of pending retried writes
F 11 1 rdata_64byt_nointv_en
DESC Enables no interleaving property on normal memory read data within 64B granule when set
F 12 3 wrt_crdgnt_weight
DESC Determines weight of credit grant allocated to retried writes in presence of pending retried reads
F 15 1 dsa_en
DESC Enables Direct Subordinate Access feature to SBSX/MTSX. When setting this bit, dis_compack_on_writes must be set to 1, because dsa mode does not work with compack flow. Requires POR_DSA_EN_PARAM to be set, otherwise this config bit has no effect.
F 16 10 max_rrt_outstd_chitxn_cnt
DESC Maximum number of outstanding reads allowed on CHI-side
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM
F 28 10 max_wrt_outstd_chitxn_cnt
DESC Maximum number of outstanding writes allowed on CHI-side
PAR RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM
F 38 1 dis_awid_to_hni_hnp_cxra
DESC If set, disables compressed AWID to HNI, HNP and CXRA, also disables compressed AWID based ordering. Set this bit if uniq-ID write performance is needed.
F 43 4 chip_id
DESC Configurable ChipID for this RNX instance. Must be correctly set for proper handling of remote traffic to HNI/HNP. Only supports values 0..3.  Two MSB's is reserved.
F 47 3 local_wrdc_timeout
DESC Configurable write data cancel timeout value for local traffic. 3'b000 -  ~2000 cycles 3'b001 -  ~4000 cycles 3'b010 -  ~8000 cylces (default) 3'b011 - ~16000 cycles 3'b100 - ~32000 cycles (all other values rsvd)
F 50 3 remote_wrdc_timeout
DESC Configurable write data cancel timeout value for remote traffic. 3'b000 -  ~2000 cycles 3'b001 -  ~4000 cycles 3'b010 -  ~8000 cylces 3'b011 - ~16000 cycles (default) 3'b100 - ~32000 cycles (all other values rsvd)
R 0xa08 64 - ROOT por_rni_cfg_ctl2
RESET 0x201 0x3ffff
DESC Functions as the configuration control register. Specifies the current mode.
RGO por_rni_rcr.cfg_ctl
SGO por_rni_scr.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 cbusy_rd_en
DESC Enables CBusy throttling of read txreq within the RNI
F 1 2 cbusy_rd_txreq_limit_inc
DESC Dynamic read TXREQ limit increment. Controls how quickly the dynamic read TXREQ limit is increased when CBusy indicates values less than 2. The possible values are: 2'b00 -  4 (default) 2'b01 -  2 2'b10 -  8 2'b11 - 16
F 3 2 cbusy_rd_txreq_limit_dec
DESC Dynamic read TXREQ limit decrement. Controls how quickly the dynamic read TXREQ limit is decreased when CBusy indicates a value of 3. The possible values are: 2'b00 -  4 (default) 2'b01 -  2 2'b10 -  8 2'b11 - 16
F 5 2 cbusy_rd_filter_threshold
DESC Fraction of CBusy read responses in the sampling window necessary to be considered valid sample of that CBusy value. The possible values are: 2'b00 - 1/16 (default) 2'b01 - 1/32 2'b10 -  1/8 2'b11 -  1/4
F 7 2 cbusy_rd_filter_window
DESC Number of CBusy read responses in one sampling window. The possible values are: 2'b00 - 256 (default) 2'b01 -  64 2'b10 - 128 2'b11 - 512
F 9 1 cbusy_wr_en
DESC Enables CBusy throttling of write txreq within the RNI
F 10 2 cbusy_wr_txreq_limit_inc
DESC Dynamic write TXREQ limit increment. Controls how quickly the dynamic write TXREQ limit is increased when CBusy indicates values less than 2. The possible values are: 2'b00 -  4 (default) 2'b01 -  2 2'b10 -  8 2'b11 - 16
F 12 2 cbusy_wr_txreq_limit_dec
DESC Dynamic write TXREQ limit decrement. Controls how quickly the dynamic write TXREQ limit is decreased when CBusy indicates a value of 3. The possible values are: 2'b00 -  4 (default) 2'b01 -  2 2'b10 -  8 2'b11 - 16
F 14 2 cbusy_wr_filter_threshold
DESC Fraction of CBusy write responses in the sampling window necessary to be considered valid sample of that CBusy value. The possible values are: 2'b00 - 1/16 (default) 2'b01 - 1/32 2'b10 -  1/8 2'b11 -  1/4
F 16 2 cbusy_wr_filter_window
DESC Number of CBusy write responses in one sampling window. The possible values are: 2'b00 - 256 (default) 2'b01 -  64 2'b10 - 128 2'b11 - 512
R 0xa10 64 - ROOT por_rni_aux_ctl
RESET 0x4004012 0x3bfff7ffff7
DESC Functions as the auxiliary control register for RN-I.
F 0 1 cg_disable
DESC Disables clock gating when set
F 1 1 ar_byp_en
DESC AR bypass enable; enables bypass path in the AR pipeline
F 2 1 park_port_arb_ptr
DESC Parks the AXI port arbitration pointer for Burst
F 4 1 upstrm_datcheck_en
DESC Upstream supports Datacheck
PAR POR_DATACHECK_EN_PARAM
F 5 1 dis_stash_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered WrUniqStash when set
F 6 1 dis_hni_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to HNI when set
F 7 1 dis_pci_cxra_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to PCI-CXRA when set
F 8 1 dis_misc_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes with following attributes when set : Device memory or EWA=0 or Excl=1
F 9 1 en_wrstream_data_dispatch_on_prior_completions
DESC If set, data dispatch for streaming writes waits for completion of all older writes
F 10 1 dis_wr_stream_on_tgttype_mismatch
DESC If set, serializes first write when moving from one tgttype to another
F 11 1 never_send_wr_full_op
DESC If set, RNI will never send WR FULL op. All write ops will be of PTL type
F 12 1 dis_tnl_burst_early_dealloc_opt
DESC If set, disables the optimization related to early deallocation of tunnelled writes for intermediate txns of burst
F 13 1 dis_data_chunking
DESC If set, disables the data chunking feature
F 14 1 dis_compack_on_writes
DESC If set, disables comp_ack on streaming writes. WrData is used for ordering writes
F 15 1 dis_rreq_bypass
DESC If set, disables read request bypass path
F 16 1 dis_rdata_bypass
DESC If set, disables read data bypass path
F 17 1 dis_ra_2hop_serial_wr_opt
DESC If set, disables 2 hop indication to ra for serilized writes; will indicate 3 hop
F 18 1 dis_pcrdgnt_bank_starv_prot
DESC If set, disables across arslice starvation protection
F 19 1 dis_size_optimization_for_32b_incr
DESC If set, disables the size related optimization for a 32B INCR burst (rh-2512). Only applies to writes.
F 20 1 dis_hnp_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to HNP when set
F 21 1 dis_pci_cxra_rd_burst
DESC If set, disables read burst to PCI-CXRA on CHI request flits . Read burst on CHI is supported only in non-decoupled RDB configuration.
F 22 1 dis_hnp_rd_burst
DESC If set, disables read burst to HNP on CHI request flits . Read burst on CHI is supported only in non-decoupled RDB configuration.
F 24 1 dis_be_all_ones_hint
DESC If set, disables hint to HNF which signals all BE=1's on writes
F 25 1 dis_ncwr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered non-cacheable writes when set
F 26 1 dis_pcie_to_lcn
DESC If set, all pcie traffic sent directly to HNF/CCG, bypasses LCN. Only has effect when pcie_mstr_present
F 27 6 clstr_intlv_mask
DESC Encoded static mask for max interleave granularity supported. When this setting is less than or equal to rnsam's programmed interleave granularity for a write to pci_cxra, tunneling/2hop flow will be used. 6'b111111: 64B 6'b111110: 128B 6'b111100: 256B 6'b111000: 512B 6'b110000: 1024B 6'b100000: 2048B 6'b000000: 4096B others:    Reserved
F 33 1 dis_pci_cxra_logical_tgt_2hop
DESC If set, disables tunneling/2hop for case where physical and logical target is pci_cxra, otherwise tunneling/2hop to RA.
F 34 1 dis_hnf_logical_tgt_2hop
DESC If set, disables tunneling/2hop for case where physical target is pci_cxra and logical target is hnf, otherwise may tunneling/2hop to RA if interleaving granularity settings allow.
F 35 1 dis_readonce_rd_burst
DESC If set, disables read burst for ReadOnce from AXI.
F 36 1 serialize_on_sameid_tgtid_change
DESC If set, serializes request issue for sameid writes to cxra when tgtid mismatches previous write reuquest.
F 37 1 memattr_cache_alloc_ovr
DESC If set, overrides the incoming memattr cacheable and allocate attributes both to 1 for non-device and bufferable requests.
F 39 1 sys_dis_data_interleaving
DESC System optimized disable read DATA interleaving for all ports. Disables all read data interleaving, including atomic read data being returned for all AXI ports.  Read burst preservation is enabled same as in normal mode, but this requires certain system level restrictions: 1. Cannot set SYS_DIS_DATA_INTERLEAVING for multi-chip systems. Support for remote HN-P is a future feature. 2. When setting SYS_DIS_DATA_INTERLEAVING for an RN-I/RN-D it is required for that RN-I/RN-D to target only one HN-P with read bursts. It is also required for the path to a single remote HN-P, when remote support is available, to only go through a single CCG and for the ccg_rni to also have SYS_DIS_DATA_INTERLEAVING set. 3. The AXI subordinate downstream of HN-P must not interleave read burst data. 4. Must have NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM==NUM_RD_BUF_PARAM and NUM_RD_REQ_PRAM<=256, otherwise this bit has no effect. 5. The sum of the maximum number of beats of a cracked burst per each port must fit wholly within an arslice - breaking this rule will result in a hang. Must comprehend DIS_PORT_TOKEN AND QPC15_ENTRY_RSV settings, which will limit number of available entries
F 40 1 disable_owo_property
DESC When set RN-I AXI interface will behave as if AXI Ordered_Write_Observation property is disabled for all writes.
F 41 1 dis_nonpci_cxra_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to (non-PCI)-CXRA when set
R 0xa18 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_port_control
RESET 0x0 0x7fffffff
DESC Controls port S0 AXI/ACE subordinate interface settings.
RGO por_rni_rcr.port_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s0_lpid_mask
DESC Port S0 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 8 s0_rd_token
DESC Port S0 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_SLICE_REQ) per slice on AR achnnel
F 19 8 s0_wr_token
DESC Port S0 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_REQ) on AW achnnel
F 27 1 s0_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS0 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request If setting cfg_ctl.wfc bit along with this bit, aux_ctl.dis_rreq_bypass must also be set, otherwise completion order will be violated.
F 28 1 s0_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port0 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RNI.
F 29 1 s0_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC. This affects RNI AR channel only.
F 30 1 s0_its_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC for non-PCIE case. This affects RNI AW channel only.
R 0xa20 64 - ROOT por_rni_s1_port_control
RESET 0x0 0x7fffffff
DESC Controls port S1 AXI/ACE subordinate interface settings.
RGO por_rni_rcr.port_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s1_lpid_mask
DESC Port S1 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 8 s1_rd_token
DESC Port S1 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_SLICE_REQ) per slice on AR achnnel
F 19 8 s1_wr_token
DESC Port S1 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_REQ) on AW achnnel
F 27 1 s1_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS1 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request If setting cfg_ctl.wfc bit along with this bit, aux_ctl.dis_rreq_bypass must also be set, otherwise completion order will be violated.
F 28 1 s1_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port1 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RNI.
F 29 1 s1_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC. This affects RNI AR channel only.
F 30 1 s1_its_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC for non-PCIE case. This affects RNI AW channel only.
R 0xa28 64 - ROOT por_rni_s2_port_control
RESET 0x0 0x7fffffff
DESC Controls port S2 AXI/ACE subordinate interface settings.
RGO por_rni_rcr.port_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s2_lpid_mask
DESC Port S2 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 8 s2_rd_token
DESC Port S2 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_SLICE_REQ) per slice on AR achnnel
F 19 8 s2_wr_token
DESC Port S2 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_XRT_REQ) on AW achnnel
F 27 1 s2_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS2 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request If setting cfg_ctl.wfc bit along with this bit, aux_ctl.dis_rreq_bypass must also be set, otherwise completion order will be violated.
F 28 1 s2_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port2 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RNI.
F 29 1 s2_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC. This affects RNI AR channel only.
F 30 1 s2_its_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk manager present such as TCU or GIC for non-PCIE case. This affects RNI AW channel only.
R 0xa30 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_mpam_control
RESET 0x0 0xff0fff15
DESC Controls port S0 AXI/ACE subordinate interface MPAM override values
RGO por_rni_rcr.mpam_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.mpam_ctrl
F 0 1 s0_mpam_override_en
DESC Port S0 MPAM override en When set, MPAM value on CHI side is driven from MPAM override value in this register. Note that when RNID_AXMPAM_EN_PARAM is set to 0, MPAM override value is always used irrespective of this bit value
F 2 1 s0_mpam_nse
DESC Port S0 MPAM_NSE value
F 4 1 s0_mpam_ns
DESC Port S0 MPAM_NS value
F 8 12 s0_mpam_partid
DESC Port S0 MPAM_PARTID value
F 24 8 s0_mpam_pmg
DESC Port S0 MPAM_PMG value
R 0xa38 64 - ROOT por_rni_s1_mpam_control
RESET 0x0 0xff0fff15
DESC Controls port S1 AXI/ACE subordinate interface MPAM override values
RGO por_rni_rcr.mpam_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.mpam_ctrl
F 0 1 s1_mpam_override_en
DESC Port S1 MPAM override en When set, MPAM value on CHI side is driven from MPAM override value in this register. Note that when RNID_AXMPAM_EN_PARAM is set to 0, MPAM override value is always used irrespective of this bit value
F 2 1 s1_mpam_nse
DESC Port S1 MPAM_NSE value
F 4 1 s1_mpam_ns
DESC Port S1 MPAM_NS value
F 8 12 s1_mpam_partid
DESC Port S1 MPAM_PARTID value
F 24 8 s1_mpam_pmg
DESC Port S1 MPAM_PMG value
R 0xa40 64 - ROOT por_rni_s2_mpam_control
RESET 0x0 0xff0fff15
DESC Controls port S2 AXI/ACE subordinate interface MPAM override values
RGO por_rni_rcr.mpam_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.mpam_ctrl
F 0 1 s2_mpam_override_en
DESC Port S2 MPAM override en When set, MPAM value on CHI side is driven from MPAM override value in this register. Note that when RNID_AXMPAM_EN_PARAM is set to 0, MPAM override value is always used irrespective of this bit value
F 2 1 s2_mpam_nse
DESC Port S2 MPAM_NSE value
F 4 1 s2_mpam_ns
DESC Port S2 MPAM_NS value
F 8 12 s2_mpam_partid
DESC Port S2 MPAM_PARTID value
F 24 8 s2_mpam_pmg
DESC Port S2 MPAM_PMG value
R 0xa80 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_qos_control
RESET 0x0 0xff00ff
DESC Controls QoS settings for port S0 AXI/ACE subordinate interface.
RGO por_rni_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 1 s0_aw_lat_en
DESC Enables port S0 AW QoS regulation when set
F 1 1 s0_ar_lat_en
DESC Enables port S0 AR QoS regulation when set
F 2 1 s0_aw_qos_override_en
DESC Enables port S0 AW QoS override; when set, allows QoS value on inbound AW transactions to be overridden
F 3 1 s0_ar_qos_override_en
DESC Enables port S0 AR QoS override; when set, allows QoS value on inbound AR transactions to be overridden
F 4 1 s0_aw_reg_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for write transactions 1'b0: Latency mode 1'b1: Period mode; used for bandwidth regulation
F 5 1 s0_ar_reg_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for read transactions 1'b0: Latency mode 1'b1: Period mode; used for bandwidth regulation
F 6 1 s0_aw_pqv_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for write transactions during period mode 1'b0: Normal mode; QoS value is stable when the manager is idle 1'b1: Quiesce high mode; QoS value tends to the maximum value when the manager is idle
F 7 1 s0_ar_pqv_mode
DESC Configures the QoS regulator mode for read transactions during period mode 1'b0: Normal mode; QoS value is stable when the manager is idle 1'b1: Quiesce high mode; QoS value tends to the maximum value when the manager is idle
F 16 4 s0_aw_qos_override
DESC AW QoS override value for port S0
F 20 4 s0_ar_qos_override
DESC AR QoS override value for port S0
R 0xa88 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_qos_lat_tgt
RESET 0x0 0xfff0fff
DESC Controls QoS target latency (in cycles) for regulations of port S0 read and write transactions.
RGO por_rni_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 12 s0_aw_lat_tgt
DESC Port S0 AW channel target latency; a value of 0 corresponds to no regulation
F 16 12 s0_ar_lat_tgt
DESC Port S0 AR channel target latency; a value of 0 corresponds to no regulation
R 0xa90 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_qos_lat_scale
RESET 0x0 0x707
DESC Controls the QoS target latency scale factor for port S0 read and write transactions. This register represents powers of two from the range 2^(-5) to 2^(-12); it is used to match a 16-bit integrator.
RGO por_rni_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 3 s0_aw_lat_scale
DESC Port S0 AW QoS scale factor 3'b000: 2^(-5) 3'b001: 2^(-6) 3'b010: 2^(-7) 3'b011: 2^(-8) 3'b100: 2^(-9) 3'b101: 2^(-10) 3'b110: 2^(-11) 3'b111: 2^(-12)
F 8 3 s0_ar_lat_scale
DESC Port S0 AR QoS scale factor 3'b000: 2^(-5) 3'b001: 2^(-6) 3'b010: 2^(-7) 3'b011: 2^(-8) 3'b100: 2^(-9) 3'b101: 2^(-10) 3'b110: 2^(-11) 3'b111: 2^(-12)
R 0xa98 64 - ROOT por_rni_s0_qos_lat_range
RESET 0x0 0xf0f0f0f
DESC Controls the minimum and maximum QoS values generated by the QoS latency regulator for port S0 read and write transactions.
RGO por_rni_rcr.qos_ctrl
SGO por_rni_scr.qos_ctrl
F 0 4 s0_aw_lat_min_qos
DESC Port S0 AW QoS minimum value
F 8 4 s0_aw_lat_max_qos
DESC Port S0 AW QoS maximum value
F 16 4 s0_ar_lat_min_qos
DESC Port S0 AR QoS minimum value
F 24 4 s0_ar_lat_max_qos
DESC Port S0 AR QoS maximum value
R 0xaa0 64 - ROOT por_rni_s1_qos_control
RESET 0x0 0xff00ff
