F 59 3 hnf_cal_override_map_11
DESC configuration to map the CAL override 2'b11 to the custom 3bit value
F 56 3 hnf_cal_override_map_10
DESC configuration to map the CAL override 2'b10 to the custom 3bit value
F 53 3 hnf_cal_override_map_01
DESC configuration to map the CAL override 2'b01 to the custom 3bit value
F 50 3 hnf_cal_override_map_00
DESC configuration to map the CAL override 2'b00 to the custom 3bit value
F 49 1 hnf_cal_bit_override
DESC configuration to choose lsb/msb bit to override device id for htg 0 1'b0: hash msb bit to override device id 1'b1: hash lsb bit to override device id
F 48 1 hnf_cal_type
DESC Enables type of HN CAL for HTG 0 1'b0: CAL2 mode 1'b1: CAL4 mode
F 47 1 hnf_cal_mode_en
DESC Enables support for HN CAL for HTG 0
F 43 4 hier_cluster_mask
DESC Hierarchical hashing: Enable cluster masking to achieve different interleave granularity across clusters. 4'b0000: 64   byte interleave granularity across clusters 4'b0110: 4096 byte interleave granularity across clusters 4'b1111: Cluster interleaving disabled others: Reserved
F 42 1 misc_tgtid_sel
DESC Select the TgtID's from HNF or Misc tgt tables 1'b0: Default, selects from HNF table 1'b1: selects from Misc Tgt table
F 35 6 hier_hash_nodes
DESC Hierarchical hashing mode, define number of nodes in each cluster
F 28 6 hier_hash_clusters
DESC Hierarchical hashing mode, define number of clusters groups
F 24 3 hier_enable_address_striping
DESC Hierarchical hashing: configure number of address bits needs to shuttered (removed) at second hierarchy hash (LSB bit is based on cluster mask). 3'b000: no address shuttering 3'b001: one addr bit shuttered   (2  clusters) 3'b010: two addr bit shuttered   (4  clusters) 3'b011: three addr bit shuttered (8  clusters) 3'b100: four addr bit shuttered  (16 clusters) 3'b101: five addr bit shuttered  (32 clusters) 3'b110: six addr bit shuttered   (These are configured when the cachelines are > 64B interleaved and clusters are enabled) 3'b111: seven addr bit shuttered others: Reserved
F 23 1 hierarchical_hash_en
DESC Hierarchical Hashing mode enable configure bit
F 22 1 nonpowerof2_hash_en
DESC Non power of two Hashing mode enable cconfigure bit
F 12 8 hnf_base_index
DESC base index to the HNF target ID table
F 2 8 num_hnf
DESC HN count for LCN group
F 1 1 lcn_tgtid_override_by_hnf_en
DESC When enabled, If LCN and HNF belong to the SAME NUCA, then LCN TgtID is overridden with HNF TgtID. This scheme eliminates LCN & HNF hoping within the same NUCA. Needs additional configurations from HNS. Disable case, Cacheline is always directed to LCN TgtID.
F 0 1 valid
DESC LCN HTG valid 1'b0: Not valid 1'b1: Valid
